[DESIGN]
UID: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-002
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template safety-critical component
TYPE: DESIGN
DESIGN_TYPE: Component
DESIGN_DEPTH: Deep
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: SafetyCritical
STATEMENT: The safety controller implements the allocated protective-stop logic, diagnostics, safe-state command, reset handling, and restart inhibition.
RATIONALE: The component directly implements REQ-TEMPLATE-SAFE-001 and SAFE-TEMPLATE-FUNC-001.
SAFETY_BOUNDARY: >>>
Boundary: Template safety boundary
Allocated safety requirement: REQ-TEMPLATE-SAFE-001
Allocated safety function: SAFE-TEMPLATE-FUNC-001
Trusted dependencies: Replace with justified dependencies
Untrusted dependencies: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-001
Required integrity target: Replace with the derived target
Response-time allocation: Replace with the allocated time
Safe state: Hazardous motion commanded to the validated safe state
<<<
INTERFERENCE_CONTROLS: >>>
Input validation: Schema, range, freshness, sequence, and state validation
Output constraints: Bounded commands and independently enforced safe-state behavior
Diagnostics: Required faults are detected within allocated diagnostic times
Watchdogs: Independent watchdog behavior is defined and verified
Fault containment: Fault effects do not propagate outside justified boundaries
Configuration protection: Safety parameters are versioned, authorized, and integrity checked
Reset and restart: Faults remain latched where required and restart requires deliberate action
<<<
CONSTRAINTS: Replace with hardware, software, environmental, timing, integrity, diagnostic, interface, and certification constraints.
CONSEQUENCES: Changes require safety-impact analysis and may invalidate component, integration, validation, and release evidence.
TAGS: template, component, safety-critical
