[DESIGN]
UID: DES-TEMPLATE-IF-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template safety-boundary interface
TYPE: DESIGN
DESIGN_TYPE: Interface
DESIGN_DEPTH: Deep
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: SafetyRelated
STATEMENT: The interface permits bounded operational requests from the communications component to the safety controller without allowing the communications component to violate the protective-stop requirement.
RATIONALE: The cross-boundary interaction is required for operation but must not transfer unrestricted safety authority.
SAFETY_BOUNDARY: >>>
Boundary crossed: Template safety boundary
Inside component: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-002
Outside component: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-001
Protected requirement: REQ-TEMPLATE-SAFE-001
Protected function: SAFE-TEMPLATE-FUNC-001
Trust assumption: All outside input is untrusted
Containment objective: Invalid or absent input cannot prevent the safe response
<<<
INTERFERENCE_CONTROLS: >>>
Schema and range validation: Required
Freshness and sequence validation: Required
Authentication and authorization: Required for privileged operations
Command arbitration: Safety state has priority over operational requests
Rate and resource limits: Explicitly bounded
Timeout: Explicitly bounded
Safe fallback: Defined independently of the outside component
Startup and shutdown: Safe defaults apply
Reset and recovery: Outside input cannot clear a latched safety condition
Update compatibility: Version mismatch is detected and handled safely
Diagnostics: Invalid, stale, and rejected input is observable
<<<
INTERFACE_CONTRACT: >>>
Provider: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-001
Consumer: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-002
Direction: Request to controller and bounded status response
Protocol and version: Replace with the approved protocol baseline
Inputs and outputs: Replace with versioned message definitions
Units and encoding: Explicit for every numeric field
Validity rules: Schema, range, state, authorization, and integrity
Freshness: Replace with maximum age
Ordering: Define sequence and duplication behavior
Maximum rate: Replace with bounded rate
Maximum latency: Replace with allocated latency
Timeout: Replace with bounded timeout
Fallback: Replace with safe response
Startup state: No operational authority until compatibility is established
Reset behavior: Safety reset cannot be commanded without required conditions
Observability: Rejections, timeouts, and compatibility faults are retained
<<<
CONSTRAINTS: Latency, resource, protocol, cybersecurity, deployment, environmental, and compatibility limits must be measurable.
CONSEQUENCES: Interface changes require compatibility analysis, boundary verification, and integration regression.
TAGS: template, interface, safety-boundary
