[DESIGN]
UID: DES-TEMPLATE-DEC-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Template design decision
TYPE: DESIGN
DESIGN_TYPE: Decision
DESIGN_DEPTH: Deep
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: SafetyRelated
STATEMENT: The system shall treat all operational requests crossing the safety boundary as untrusted and shall arbitrate them below active safety responses.
RATIONALE: This prevents lower-assurance communication behavior from overriding the required safe response.
SAFETY_BOUNDARY: The decision applies to DES-TEMPLATE-IF-001 and the template safety boundary.
INTERFERENCE_CONTROLS: Validation, authorization, state gating, priority arbitration, timeout, diagnostics, and safe fallback.
CONSTRAINTS: Arbitration behavior must be deterministic and included in response-time analysis.
CONSEQUENCES: Requests may be rejected or delayed while a safety response is active.
ALTERNATIVES: >>>
Alternative A: Trust the communications component.
Alternative B: Permit direct operational command forwarding.
Alternative C: Validate and arbitrate requests in the safety controller.
Selection: Alternative C.
Selection rationale: It minimizes transferred authority and supports independent safe response.
<<<
CHANGE_IMPACT: >>>
Affected requirements: REQ-TEMPLATE-SAFE-001
Affected components: DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-001 and DES-TEMPLATE-CMP-002
Affected interfaces: DES-TEMPLATE-IF-001
Affected safety function: SAFE-TEMPLATE-FUNC-001
Required regression: Interface, arbitration, timing, robustness, and fault injection
Required approvals: Safety architecture and component authorities
<<<
